zizhan: IOMobileFramebuffer show() does not wait for the panel to take a zero-copy flip (kernel boot-arg pong_zc_async=1:
pong_scanout_frame returns 3 = flipped, latch pending). Each frame is tagged with its swap id; SwapWait asks the scanout driver which
tag has latched (a CTL_FLUSH read), so "presented"/"replaced" stay true to the panel while the presenter thread moves on to the next
frame (docs/progress/2026-11-01-zero-copy-and-return-paths.md section 7 step 1). Stacks on 0012.

